// Common Core Ontologies 2.2: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// The arrival of a fictional container vessel, the Saltmarsh Trader, at the berth of a fictional port, Eastmere, on 2
// October 2026. The data has the vessel's owner, a commercial organization, Larkspur Shipping, with its legal name,
// commercial role and capability, and the act of ownership that realizes it; the Eastmere port authority, a
// government organization within the council's government, delimited by its district; the vessel's master, who is
// employed by Larkspur, and a deckhand, who make up the crew, and a port officer, each an agent and organization
// member with a capability and roles; the vessel, with its proper name painted on the hull, its IMO number, and its
// length, measured in metres, CCO's Meter Measurement Unit; the port, on the shore, and the berth, whose spatial
// region is designated by coordinates recorded in WGS 84 latitude and longitude; the cargo voyage, whose arrival at
// the berth the master carries out in an operator role, in an interval within the day, week, month, year and decade,
// with the date recorded in the logbook; and the arrival report the master sends the port authority.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

